s></name><name><surname>George</surname><given-names>A.L.</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name><name><surname>Horn</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Molecular basis of charge movement in voltage-gated sodium channels</article-title><source>Neuron.</source><volume>16</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>122</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8562074</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Yellen1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yellen</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The moving parts of voltage-gated ion channels</article-title><source>Q. Rev. Biophys.</source><volume>31</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>239</fpage><lpage>295</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10384687</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn><p>Address correspondence to Kenton J. Swartz, Molecular Physiology and Biophysics Unit, National Institute of Neurological Disorders and Stroke, National Institutes of Health, Building 36, Room 2C19, 36 Convent Drive, MSC 4066, Bethesda, MD 20892. Fax: (301) 435-5666&#x0003b; E-mail: <email>swartzk@ninds.nih.gov</email></p></fn><fn><p><italic>Abbreviations used in this paper:</italic> &#x003b1;-PI, &#x003b1;-periodicity index&#x0003b; TM, transmembrane.</p></fn></fn-group></back><floats-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Gating Properties of Wild-type and Mutant drk1 K<sup>+</sup> Channels</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr valign="bottom" align="center"><th/><th>V<sub>50</sub></th><th>z</th><th>&#x00394;G<sub>0</sub></th><th>&#x00394;&#x00394;G<sub>0</sub></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr valign="bottom" align="center"><td/><td>mV</td><td/><td>kcal/mol</td><td>kcal/mol</td></tr><tr valign="bottom"><td align="left">WT</td><td align="char" char=".">&#x02212;1.5 &#x000b1; 0.30</td><td align="char" char=".">2.7 &#x000b1; 0.028</td><td align="char